{"file":"swagger-contract-testing-1.2.0-v2.zip","bytes":227033,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"swagger-contract-testing","description":"Expert assistant for PactFlow and Pact contract testing — consumer-driven contracts, provider verification, can-i-deploy, BDCT, Drift CLI, and OpenAPI spec parsing. Includes specialized agents for reviewing and generating pact tests.","version":"1.2.0"},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"swagger-contract-testing","description":"Expert assistant for PactFlow and Pact contract testing — consumer-driven contracts, provider verification, can-i-deploy, BDCT, Drift CLI, and OpenAPI spec parsing. Includes specialized agents for reviewing and generating pact tests.","version":"1.2.0"},{"path":"plugin.json","name":"swagger-contract-testing","description":"Expert assistant for PactFlow and Pact contract testing — consumer-driven contracts, provider verification, can-i-deploy, BDCT, Drift CLI, and OpenAPI spec parsing. Includes specialized agents for reviewing and generating pact tests.","version":"1.2.0","repository":"https://github.com/pactflow/pactflow-agent-skills","homepage":"https://github.com/pactflow/pactflow-agent-skills"}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/drift-testing/SKILL.md","name":"drift-testing","description":"Verifies API implementations against OpenAPI specifications using the Drift CLI, catching spec drift and supporting Bi-Directional Contract Testing (BDCT). Use when the user mentions Drift, API contract testing, provider contract testing, provider verification, spec drift, API conformance testing, OpenAPI verification, BDCT, drift expressions, drift datasets, drift lifecycle hooks, or Lua scripting in a testing context. Use when the user asks to write, run, or debug Drift test cases. Use when the user wants to test their API against an OpenAPI spec, generate tests from an OpenAPI spec, or check whether their API has drifted from its spec. Use when the user wants full endpoint coverage, wants all tests to pass, or asks to \"keep running until everything passes\".","headings":["Drift Skill","Reference Files","Scripts","Installation","Quickest — no install needed","Project-level (recommended for teams)","Global","Verify","Project Setup","yaml-language-server: $schema=https://download.pactflow.io/drift/schemas/drift.testcases.v1.schema.json","Running Tests","Basic run","Single operation (fast iteration)","Re-run only failures","Filter by tags","Full Coverage Feedback Loop","Step 0 — Check current coverage","Run against your spec and test file(s)"],"name_hint":"drift · testing","description_zh":"使用 Drift CLI 对照 OpenAPI 规范验证 API 实现，发现实现与规格的偏移并支持双向契约测试 BDCT。适用于编写、运行和调试 Drift 用例、表达式、数据集、生命周期钩子及测试中的 Lua 脚本，以及从规范生成测试和检查端点覆盖。"},{"path":"skills/oas-generator/SKILL.md","name":"oas-generator","description":"Generates an OpenAPI 3.x YAML spec from a provider codebase using ripwire when no spec exists. Invoke this skill whenever the user needs an OpenAPI spec for a service that doesn't have one published — phrases like \"generate an openapi spec from the code\", \"there's no oas for this service\", \"create a spec from the codebase\", \"the provider doesn't have a spec\", or any time a pact-coverage or contract testing workflow is blocked because the provider spec is missing. Uses ripwire to extract HTTP route definitions and handler schemas across Ruby (Rails/Sinatra), Node.js (Express/Fastify), Python (Flask/FastAPI), and other ripwire-supported languages. Always ask for the codebase path if not provided. Requires ripwire on PATH.","headings":["OAS Generator","Step 1 — Identify the framework","Step 2 — Extract all routes","Ruby — Rails","Ruby — Sinatra","Node.js — Express / Fastify / Koa","Python — Flask","Python — FastAPI","Fallback — any language","Step 3 — Build the route inventory","Step 4 — Extract schemas per route","Step 5 — Assemble the OpenAPI YAML","Step 6 — Write and report","Tips for accuracy"],"name_hint":"oas · generator","description_zh":"在服务没有已发布规范时，使用 ripwire 从提供方代码库提取 HTTP 路由和处理器模式，生成 OpenAPI 3.x YAML。支持 Rails／Sinatra、Express／Fastify、Flask／FastAPI 等 ripwire 支持的语言框架；需要代码库路径和 PATH 中可用的 ripwire，适用于契约测试因缺少规范而受阻的场景。"},{"path":"skills/openapi-parser/SKILL.md","name":"openapi-parser","description":"Parses complex OpenAPI specs and generates Drift test cases from them. Use whenever the user wants to generate, write, or scaffold Drift tests from an OpenAPI spec — especially when the spec contains complex schemas: anyOf/oneOf/allOf, discriminators, polymorphism, inheritance, $ref chains, regex patterns, enums, or optional fields. Use when the user asks to \"create tests for an endpoint\", \"cover all response variants\", \"generate test cases from the spec\", or says anything like \"each viable combination of responses\". Use when the user is trying to understand what values are valid for a complex schema field, or when they paste a spec path and ask what tests to write.","headings":["OpenAPI Parser Skill","Reference files","Workflow","1. Locate the endpoint","Find the line number of the endpoint (macOS/Linux/Git Bash/WSL)","Read just that block (adjust line range as needed)","Then follow each $ref to components/schemas","PowerShell equivalents (Windows)","2. Resolve $refs recursively","3. Enumerate viable combinations","4. Generate Drift test cases","5. Output format","Example"],"name_hint":"openapi · parser","description_zh":"解析复杂 OpenAPI 规范并生成 Drift 测试，覆盖 anyOf／oneOf／allOf、判别器、多态、继承、引用链、正则、枚举和可选字段。适用于理解复杂字段的合法值、为端点生成用例及覆盖可行的响应组合。"},{"path":"skills/pact-coverage/SKILL.md","name":"pact-coverage","description":"Runs a coverage check to find which API operations, status codes, request body required fields, and response body required fields are NOT exercised by existing Pact consumer tests. Invoke this skill whenever the user asks \"what's not covered by my pacts?\", \"which endpoints are missing pact tests?\", \"do my pact files cover the full spec?\", \"how complete is my pact coverage?\", \"which required fields aren't tested?\", or any time they have Pact v2/v3/v4 JSON files and want to measure contract test coverage against an OpenAPI spec. Also invoke when they say they want to improve pact coverage or find coverage gaps — even if they don't say \"pact-coverage\" explicitly. Do NOT invoke for running provider verification, publishing pacts to a broker, or checking can-i-deploy; use the pactflow skill for those.","headings":["Pact Coverage","What this measures","ripwire MCP setup","→ claude mcp add ripwire -- ripwire --mcp","OpenAPI spec selection","After validation — you MUST follow one of these three paths and no others:","Pact file resolution","Pact file selection","Consumer codebase path","Running coverage","Interpreting the report","Filling gaps","Scripts (CI / advanced)","Step 1: discover consumer routes (Strategy 1 only — simple consumers)","Step 2: filter provider OAS + measure coverage (Sections 1-4)","With Section 5 (consumer code status branch analysis)","Fetch pacts from broker directly (no local files needed)"],"name_hint":"pact · coverage","description_zh":"将现有 Pact v2／v3／v4 JSON 消费者测试与 OpenAPI 规范比较，找出未覆盖的 API 操作、状态码及请求和响应必填字段，支持契约测试覆盖率评估和缺口改进。提供方验证、发布至 broker 及 can-i-deploy 检查由 pactflow 处理。"},{"path":"skills/pactflow/SKILL.md","name":"pactflow","description":"Expert assistant for PactFlow and Pact contract testing. Use this skill whenever the user mentions PactFlow, Pact, contract testing, consumer-driven contracts, provider verification, can-i-deploy, pact broker, pacticipants, bi-directional contract testing (BDCT), publishing pacts, recording deployments, provider states, the contract matrix, or managing environments and versions in a PactFlow workspace. Also trigger when the user wants to generate or review Pact tests using AI, check deployment safety, investigate why a consumer-provider verification failed, or integrate contract testing into CI/CD. Trigger even if the user doesn't say \"PactFlow\" explicitly — phrases like \"safe to deploy?\", \"check compatibility between services\", \"consumer test\", \"OpenAPI contract\", or \"service compatibility matrix\" are strong signals.","headings":["PactFlow & Pact Contract Testing","Setup & Configuration","Core Concepts & Theory","Writing Tests","Pact Broker & CI/CD","PactFlow & MCP Tools","MCP Setup","Core Concepts","Standard Pact Workflow","PactFlow AI Features (Cloud only)","Diagnosing Can-i-deploy Failures","Writing Consumer Tests and Provider Verification","Other Diagnostic Patterns","Workspace Management","Deployment vs Release","Tool Naming"],"name_hint":"pactflow","description_zh":"支持 PactFlow／Pact 契约测试，涵盖消费者驱动契约、提供方验证、can-i-deploy、broker、双向契约测试、契约发布、部署记录、提供方状态、兼容矩阵及环境版本管理。可生成或审查 Pact 测试、诊断消费者与提供方验证失败，并接入 CI/CD。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[],"mcp_servers":["smartbear","smartbear"],"config_names":["pact_broker_base_url","pact_broker_token","pact_broker_base_url","pact_broker_token"],"paths":[".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".codex-plugin/plugin.json",".mcp.json","agents/bdct-tester.md","agents/pact-coverage.md","agents/pact-generator.md","agents/pact-implementor.md","agents/pact-maintainer.md","agents/pact-reviewer.md","hooks/check-pact-config.sh","hooks/deployment-reminder.sh","hooks/hooks.json","mcp.json","plugin.json","skills/drift-testing/SKILL.md","skills/drift-testing/evals/01-basic-get-endpoint.json","skills/drift-testing/evals/02-stateful-delete-endpoint.json","skills/drift-testing/evals/03-debug-failing-test.json","skills/drift-testing/evals/fixtures/products-api-with-failures.md","skills/drift-testing/evals/fixtures/simple-products-api.yaml","skills/drift-testing/references/auth.md","skills/drift-testing/references/cli-reference.md","skills/drift-testing/references/lua-api.md","skills/drift-testing/references/mock-server.md","skills/drift-testing/references/pactflow-and-cicd.md","skills/drift-testing/references/test-cases.md","skills/drift-testing/scripts/check_coverage.py","skills/drift-testing/scripts/extract_endpoints.py","skills/drift-testing/sc